    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d538">

                <pb facs="0662" n="577" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg577"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">312.93/182</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chinese Chargé</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Yung
                            Kwai</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-10-01"><hi rendition="#italic">October 1,
                        1919</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The Secretary of State presents his compliments to the Chinese Chargé d’Affaires,
                    and, referring to his memorandum of September 24, 1919, relative to protection
                    for Chinese citizens in Mexico, has the honor to inform the Chinese Chargé
                    d’Affaires that all American Consular Officers in Mexico have been
                    telegraphically instructed, in cases of necessity, to exercise their informal
                    good offices with local Mexican authorities in behalf of Chinese citizens in
                    their Districts seeking protection.<anchor n="56" xml:id="d538-f1"/></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
